# f1 = label, f2 = more, f3 = same
# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# Where the build verifies, an operation that stands for one of the input takes, at each operand, what lies within the row of the input operand's maker
# (Walker::takesWhatRowOfInputOperandCannotGive(), walk/AOTWalk.cpp): an Add over a ToString never becomes an Add over a number. Three things are legal and must not ring:
# a Strcat makes a text of every operand itself, so the ToString in front of it may be left out and the number kept; an operator in a form of numbers takes the truth of a comparison as 0 or 1; a strict comparison with a number reads its other operand through NumberOrNaN, and the value that is read is what is judged.
# RUN(TEXT): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# TEXT: code f1:Body
# RUN(TRUTH): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# TRUTH: code f2:Body
# TRUTH: Sub {{*}} form=Integers
# RUN(NUMBER): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# NUMBER: code f3:Body
# NUMBER: NumberOrNaN
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
